I'll solve all three parts directly. Let me note that part (b) as literally rendered ($\sqrt{3}-\cos x$) gives $\pi/\sqrt{2}$, not the stated Gamma answer; the integral consistent with the claimed value is $\int_0^\pi \frac{dx}{\sqrt{3-\cos x}}$. I verify this interpretation below.

